$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Procedure (coupling of
naphthylsulfamate SI-1 is used as an example). A 4 mL reaction vial with
a magnetic stir bar was charged with Ph-B(pin) (36.6 mg, 0.175 mmol, 0.35
equiv), anhydrous powdered NaOtBu (108.1 mg, 1.125 mmol, 2.25 equiv),
NiCl2(DME) (5.5 mg, 0.025 mmol, 5 mol %), hexamethylbenzene (8.1 mg,
0.050 mmol, 0.1 equiv), and SIPr·HCl (21.7 mg, 0.0506 mmol, 10 mol %).
Subsequently, 2-Me-THF (2.5 ml), naphthylsulfamate 4 (125.7 mg, 0.5002
mmol, 1.0 equiv), and morpholine (87.1 μL, 0.900 mmol, 1.8 equiv) were
added, sequentially. The resulting heterogenous mixture was stirred for 1
min while purging with N2, and the vial was sealed with a Teflon-lined
screw cap. The mixture was stirred at 23 °C for 1 h, and then at 80 °C
for 3 h in a preheated aluminum heating block. The reaction vessel was
allowed to cool to 23 °C and the mixture was filtered by passage over a
plug of silica gel (EtOAC eluent, 5 mL), and then concentrated under
reduced pressure. The yield was determined by 1H NMR analysis with
hexamethylbenzene as an internal standard. Spectral data match those
previously reported.6 11 (Figure 3). The yield was determined by 1H NMR
analysis with hexamethylbenzene as an internal standard. Spectral data
match those previously reported.12 Compound 11: Yield 58%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, sealed vial used, Suzuki-Miyaura coupling
reaction, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Amination of Aryl Chlorides and Sulfamates in
2-Methyl-THF
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fine Nathel, Noah F.; Kim, Junyong; Hie, Liana; Jiang, Xingyu; Garg, Neil
K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM ACS Catalysis (2014), 4(9), 3289-3293

