$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the amination reaction
of 3-bromooxindoles with racemic 3-substituted indolines and the
convertion of indoline into indole with DDQ oxidation : To a solution of
indoline 1 (0.12 mmol) in MTBE (1.5 ml), which was added to the mixture
of 3-bromooxindole 2 (0.1 mmol), DABCO (0.15 mmol) and catalyst
Ni(OAc)2-3e (0.02 mmol), the resulting solution was then stirred at room
temperature. After the starting material was completely consumed as
monitored by TLC, the mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The crude
products was purified by flash column chromatography (EA/CH2Cl2 =
1:100-1:20) to give 4. To a stirred solution of 4 in DCM was added DDQ
(1.5 eq). After stirring for 10 min at room temperature, the reaction
mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The crude products was purified by
flash column chromatography (EA/CH2Cl2 = 1:100-1:20) to give product.
(S)-methyl
2-(1-(3-(2-azidoethyl)-2-oxoindolin-3-yl)-1H-indol-3-yl)acetate.(5a)
Yield 57%, 83% ee, time: 24 h. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO) δ 11.08 (s, 1 H),
7.73 (s, 1 H), 7.48 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.35 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.12
(d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.05 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.97 (dd, J = 14.4, 7.3
Hz, 2 H), 6.87 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 6.49 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1 H), 3.80 (s,
2 H), 3.63 (s, 3 H), 3.27 (dd, J = 12.7, 5.7 Hz, 1 H), 3.22-3.05 (m, 1
H), 2.92-2.00 (m, 2 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, DMSO) δ 175.3, 171.7, 141.5,
135.2, 130.2, 128.8, 128.1, 125.4, 124.2, 122.7, 121.6, 119.4, 119.1,
110.6, 110.5, 107.6, 64.9, 51.6, 45.6, 35.1, 30.4. IR: 3270, 2925, 2100,
1733, 1483, 1264, 1017, 741, 487 cm-1; [α]25D = -56 (c 0.8, CHCl3). HRMS
(ESI): C21H19N5O3+Na, Calc: 412.1380, Found: 412.1386; HPLC: Chiralcel
OD, Hexane/iPrOH = 50/50, flow rate = 0.6 mL/min, retention time: tmajor
= 10.4, tminor = 18.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 83% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Construction of the N1-C3 Linkage Stereogenic Centers by Catalytic
Asymmetric Amination Reaction of 3-Bromooxindoles with Indolines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
